WEBVTT

00:04.903 --> 00:10.359
AI agents run commands with your permissions, on your real files.

00:10.359 --> 00:13.380
Kule puts a control room in between.

00:13.380 --> 00:16.402
Every task is a copy of your folder.

00:16.402 --> 00:23.033
The agent works in that copy, inside a sandbox, and nothing reaches your folder

00:23.033 --> 00:25.634
until you review it and commit.

00:26.835 --> 00:31.792
Start with any folder: code, notes, documents or photos.

00:31.792 --> 00:34.271
Here it is a small web shop.

00:34.271 --> 00:41.086
On macOS the copy is a clone, so it takes almost no space until files change.

00:42.289 --> 00:45.696
Then tell the agent what to do.

00:45.696 --> 00:53.060
Kule runs Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, or any agent that speaks ACP.

00:54.261 --> 00:58.449
Every tool call shows up as it happens, with what it prints.

00:58.449 --> 01:01.311
Each change is a step you can go back to.

01:01.311 --> 01:06.825
The bar under the prompt shows what the run takes of your computer, against the

01:06.825 --> 01:07.872
limits you set.

01:09.074 --> 01:13.256
Every connection goes through the task's proxy.

01:13.256 --> 01:15.391
Package registries pass.

01:15.391 --> 01:22.863
Here, a package's install script wants to reach a telemetry host the policy does not

01:22.863 --> 01:24.909
know, so Kule asks you.

01:24.909 --> 01:28.646
Deny it, and the agent goes on without it.

01:29.848 --> 01:35.929
When the run is over, Review shows what changed inside each file: methods, fields

01:35.929 --> 01:37.805
and keys, not just lines.

01:37.805 --> 01:40.132
Source edits pass on their own.

01:40.132 --> 01:46.063
package.json and the lockfile decide what gets installed, so they wait for your

01:46.063 --> 01:46.739
approval.

01:46.739 --> 01:52.219
Approve and commit, and the changes reach your folder, with a checkpoint.

01:53.421 --> 01:59.472
The timeline keeps every commit, and every connection the task made, the one you

01:59.472 --> 02:00.304
denied too.

02:00.304 --> 02:01.665
Changed your mind?

02:01.665 --> 02:03.632
Undo puts the folder back.

02:10.076 --> 02:12.668
Your API keys stay with Kule.

02:12.668 --> 02:20.087
The agent only sees a placeholder, and the proxy puts in the real key for the hosts

02:20.087 --> 02:20.892
you name.

02:20.892 --> 02:28.311
Limits hold each run to the processor, memory, disk and time you allow, and budgets

02:28.311 --> 02:30.367
cap what runs may cost.

02:31.568 --> 02:37.800
Everything the window does, the kule CLI does too, on the same tasks, so you can

02:37.800 --> 02:38.579
script it.

02:50.108 --> 02:59.782
Kule is open source, under the Apache license, and a preview for macOS and Linux.

02:59.782 --> 03:04.439
Read the docs at kulehq.github.io/kule.
